<title>LATVIA: First Latvia two-year T-bill yield 9.52 pct.</title>
<headline>First Latvia two-year T-bill yield 9.52 pct.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield at the first auction of two-year Latvian T-bills was 9.52 percent on Wednesday, the state exchequer said.</p>
<p>The two-year paper was being auctioned for the first time as the government tries to lengthen the maturity of state debt. One-year paper was previously the longest maturity.</p>
<p>Among shorter-term maturities, one-month yields rose while three-month paper slipped, it added.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of lats.</p>
<p> MATURITY    AV YLD(pct) LAST WEEK NO OF BNKS ISSUE  BID  SOLD</p>
<p> One-month    5.42	   4.49	  2	0.50   0.75 0.50</p>
<p> Three-month  5.74	   5.86	  7	 1.0   2.14  1.0</p>
<p> Two-year     9.52	   --	   12	17.0  48.32 17.0</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
